fluxecho.bee_imprinter.tip=§3Imprints every gene of a real bee, unharmed§r\nSpecial slot: the sample bee (or an imprint); it stays there\nPaper in: an imprint of all the sample's genes\nImprint + programmed circuit in: the sample's genes written onto it (species kept)\n  1 speed  2 lifespan  3 fertility  4 temperature  5 nocturnal  6 humidity\n  7 rain  8 cave  9 flower  10 pollination  11 territory  12 effect\n  13 every environment gene (4-8: no more hunting for climates)  14 every gene but the species\n%s s per run, %s EU/t
fluxecho.larva_incubator.tip=§3Feeds larvae honey drops until they grow into the imprinted bee§r\nPristine, analysed, pure-bred; climate does not matter\nSpecial slot: a bee imprint (or a real bee); it stays there\nNo circuit or circuit 1: %3$s honey drops -> 1 princess + %4$s drones\nCircuit 2: %5$s honey drops -> %6$s drones\nA princess left in the output holds the next batch\n%1$s s per batch, %2$s EU/t
